  m_overrideMarkdownText: '# Meta Model API


    Meta Model API is Meta''s developer
    API for the Muse family of models.





    While the model can be used to accomplish
    many goals, the ones outlined here are targeted toward common use cases:


    -
    Ask questions, e.g.: ''What is a synonym for chair?''

    - Make queries about
    images, e.g.: ''What is in this image: {image}''

    - Translate data, e.g.:
    ''Translate "Hello" into Vietnamese.''

    - Format data or answers into JSON


    Getting
    the desired output from an AI relies mostly on constructing "prompts" (questions
    with context) worded in particular ways to generate suitable responses.


    Multiple
    models are available with different context windows and capabilities. The Muse
    Spark family (`muse-spark-1.1` through `muse-spark-1.3`) handles text and image
    understanding through a single chat endpoint.


    For more information: <a
    href="https://ai.developer.meta.com/docs/getting-started/overview">`Meta Model
    API Docs`</a>



    ### Getting Started


    Create an Account at: <a href="https://ai.developer.meta.com/">`Meta
    Model API`</a>.


    Create an API Key to pass in requests, from the **API keys**
    tab of the dashboard. You only see the key once, so save it immediately. Keys
    start with `LLM|`. Treat the key as a secret: keep it out of source control and
    out of builds you ship (see <a href=".\Packages\com.meta.utilities.metamodelapi/#configuration">Configuration</a>).



    ##
    Common Use Cases



    ### Accurate Object Description


    The classification
    from object detection is a coarse (and sometimes incorrect) umbrella term for
    detected objects. Passing a cropped image of the subject item to the model, the
    scene description is able to provide a more accurate and descriptive summary
    of the item.



    ### Generating Lesson Data (Word Clouds)


    Passing a
    descriptive noun along with an image of the corresponding object to the scene
    description service, it is able to return a rich set of nouns, adjectives, and
    verbs.



    ### Translation


    The model is used to translate the scene
    description results into both the user''s native language and the target language,
    to facilitate translation and language learning.



    ### Speech Evaluation


    Using
    a transcription of the user''s voice, the model is used to evaluate a user''s
    response using multiple criteria, including checking for the presence of specific
    words and parts of speech (nouns, verbs, and adjectives).

'
